# 2025-11-24 17:37:50.467972
+Create a very simple two-player game called Block Grid.
+
+Show a 3x3 grid of empty squares.
+
+There are two players:
+- Player 1 uses the blue block emoji 🟦
+- Player 2 uses the red X emoji ❌
+
+Keep track of turns:
+- The first tap places 🟦
+- The second tap places ❌
+- The third tap places 🟦
+- The fourth tap places ❌
+and so on, always alternating.
+
+When the user taps on a square:
+- if the square is empty, place the current player's symbol (🟦 or ❌) in that square
+- if the square is not empty, do nothing
+
+After each move, check all rows, columns and diagonals:
+- if three squares in a line have 🟦, show the text "Blue wins!"
+- if three squares in a line have ❌, show the text "Red wins!"
+
+Add a button "Reset" that clears the grid and starts again with Player 1 (🟦).
+
+Keep the layout very simple:
+- the 3x3 grid in the centre
+- the "Blue wins!" or "Red wins!" text when there is a line
+- a small "Reset" button under the grid
+No animations, no timers, no extra features.
+

